\title{Spanning subgraph}
\date{2026-10-09T02:33:24Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\taxon{Definition}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{Let #{G = (V,E)} be an unweighted graph with vertices #{V} and
edges #{E}.  A \em{spanning subgraph} of #{G} is a [connected](00LT) graph #{V,E'} where #{E' \subseteq E}.}

\p{That is, a spanning subgraph of #{G} is a connected graph with the
same vertices as #{G} and a subset of the edges; to make a spanning subgraph of #{G} we pick some edges which connect all the vertices.}
